---
import Section from './Section.astro';
// Personal science — FDR-validated correlations + personal cutoffs. §1 calls this
// "a rigor most consumer apps don't attempt." The caffeine-cutoff example is from §1.
// The statistical method names live inside the rendered card (technical surface);
// the marketing copy stays plain — "strict enough to rule out coincidence".
---

<Section id="personal" labelledby="personal-h">
  <h2 id="personal-h" class="rise mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,3rem)]">
    Patterns from <span class="text-accent-soft">your</span> data — not a study’s.
  </h2>

  <div class="mt-10 grid items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1fr] lg:gap-16">
    <div class="rise">
      <p class="lede">
        It watches for connections in your own history, then tests each one strictly enough to rule
        out coincidence — so a “finding” is a real signal, not just something that caught your eye on
        a chart.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
        That’s a level of rigor most consumer apps don’t attempt. And a pattern in your own data is
        the strongest nudge there is — because it’s yours, not a population average pinned onto you.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure
      class="surface surface-lift rise p-6 sm:p-7"
      aria-label="Rendered example: a personal finding about late caffeine, tested to rule out coincidence"
    >
      <figcaption class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <span class="mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-ink-faint">
          Personal finding &middot; validated
        </span>
        <span class="chip chip-warn chip-dot">from your data</span>
      </figcaption>
      <hr class="hairline my-5" />
      <p class="display-line text-[1.55rem]">
        Coffee after <span class="mono">~3&thinsp;pm</span>
        <span class="text-ink-faint">&rarr;</span>
        <span class="text-accent-soft">&minus;40 min</span> sleep
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        On the nights you logged a late coffee, you slept about 40 minutes less. Measured against your
        own baseline — a pattern in your data, never a population average pinned onto you.
      </p>
      <dl class="mono mt-5 grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-x-4 gap-y-1.5 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        <dt>test</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Mann&ndash;Whitney, coincidence-corrected</dd>
        <dt>window</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">60 days</dd>
        <dt>holds</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">after ruling out chance</dd>
      </dl>
    </figure>
  </div>
</Section>
